{"body":"Credited prior answer: **already_solved, 0/5**. Matthias Franz's published big polygon spaces realize maximal nonfree syzygy order floor((r−1)/2) over Q for every requested torus rank r≥5. Odd ranks use the equilateral construction; even ranks use an additional effective circle acting on S³. The compact connected orientable smooth examples satisfy the source hypotheses. This is reconstruction and verification of prior work.\n\nThe original OWR question is checked in its rational-coefficient context against the Allday–Franz–Puppe rank bound, Franz's corrected 2023 author version of the IMRN 2015 paper, and Franz–Huang 2020. The source rank typo, Morse sign and grading corrections are recorded. No integral-coefficient, positive-characteristic, minimal-dimension or novelty claim is made.\n\nThe repair preserves all sixteen historical author/review files. It replaces three current wrappers (PUBLICATION.md, PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json, verify_publication.py) and adds six files: CURRENT_SCOPE_CORRECTION.md, CURRENT_SCOPE_MANIFEST.json, verify_corrected_source_cases.py, CORRECTED_SOURCE_CASE_CHECKS.json, review/independent_check_corrected.py, and review/CORRECTED_INDEPENDENT_CHECKS.json.\n\nThe historical guide and two historical checkers used free quotient shifts as Ext targets. At r=5, a=b=1, the actual sequence is 0→C→H→Q→0, with free target shifts 0 and 3 in C, and quotient shifts 10 and 13 in Q. Thus Ext¹(K₄[9],R[l]) uses differences −9 and −6. The corrected vanishing still gives splitting; an independent nonsplit depth argument proves the exact order without needing splitting. The preserved historical PASS outputs do not certify their wrong shift assertions. The current wrappers bind the correction and separate corrected checks. General b>1 splitting is not exported.\n\nExact repaired head: a7a6729d544f53b2be20b0e648f4001771bc2f42; parents: original head 75bea4d3be9904e90c3843892671a440ba4d2c42 and main a3cfbf7795fc8687f6029e9d00b3ec0a201934f0. Its 26 changed paths comprise the 25 target files and the queue. Only problem 30002200's status cell changes from queued to already_solved; its count stays 0/5, and every other queue byte is preserved. The earlier WIP is verified historical ancestry, not the repaired head's second parent.\n\nRoot and distinct adversarial families checked the geometric, equivariant, Koszul, product and priority arguments. A fresh source-first whole-package reviewer passed the corrected mathematics and final actual-head/object/queue/metadata gate. Root privately reproduced the full final receipt, including five byte-exact full streams, all 87 owned evidence files, 143 seal-binding instances and 42 private source artifacts. Full replay reproduces 358,064 historical author assertions and 983 historical independent controls; separate corrected and fresh checks are recorded without treating overlapping counts as distinct discoveries. Public wrappers verify zero optional PDF files; original-source verification is separately hash-bound. Source PDFs remain private.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in research, drafting, verification and adversarial review. This work is unrefereed and has not received external human peer review. Accept the verified credited outcome. The exact-head gate is complete; actual merge is recorded separately. No paper, Zenodo deposit, DOI, tracker row or release.\n\n[Acceptance decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr377_30002200/ACCEPTANCE_DECISION.md) · [fresh final adversarial audit](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr377_30002200/clean_corrected_final_adversary/FINAL_ACTUAL_HEAD_AUDIT.md).\n","headRefOid":"a7a6729d544f53b2be20b0e648f4001771bc2f42","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":{"oid":"b3b1a74df434768ee221b17eea3be22b97b4ad3c"},"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":"2026-10-03T06:55:15Z","state":"MERGED","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel